Kim: Let me show you the key finding from the study.

  The testing effect is one of the most robust findings in
  cognitive psychology:

  - Students who **tested themselves** recalled ~50% more
  - Students who **re-read** the material felt more confident
    but performed worse

  > Roediger & Karpicke, 2006

Alex: Wow, that's a big difference. [face=awe]

Kim: Before we go on, take a moment to reflect on this.

